# openccu-lite: a radio stick plugged in or pulled while the box runs (an HmIP-RFUSB, an
# HmIP-RFUSB-TK, an HB-RF-USB, an HM-CFG-USB-2). Started by the udev rule
# 61-openccu-lite-radio-hotplug.rules; `occulited radio hotplug` lists the nodes again, probes only
# the new ones (a node a daemon holds keeps the result of the boot's detection), makes the plan and
# restarts only the interface daemons whose plan changed. A stick nothing uses changes nothing but
# the results under /run/occulite/radio. It waits for the boot's detection, and stands aside while
# a coprocessor flash or a connection change of occulited runs (both re-run the detection).
[Unit]
Description=Radio stick hotplug
After=occu-init-rf-hardware.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/occulited radio hotplug
TimeoutStartSec=600
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
